What is HPLC Buffer for Amino Acid Analysis?
HPLC buffer for amino acid analysis refers to specially formulated aqueous buffer systems-commonly citrate (sodium or lithium) or phosphate salts-used as the mobile phase in ion‑exchange or reversed‑phase high‑performance liquid chromatography. By precisely controlling pH and ionic strength, these buffers enable sequential separation and accurate quantification of amino acids in protein hydrolysates, biological fluids, food matrices, and pharmaceutical preparations.
